1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:23,440
On Warren Peak in the Rockies,

2
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:28,940
a nuclear power plant is serving the Air Defense Command radar station near Sundance, Wyoming.

3
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,960
It is the PM-1 Air Transportable Nuclear Power Plant, designed and manufactured by the Martin Company.

4
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:42,380
PM-1 is a joint undertaking of the Department of the Air Force and the Army Nuclear Power Program,

5
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:44,519
a part of the Atomic Energy Commission.

6
00:00:45,399 --> 00:00:53,359
The PM-1 reactor, a compact pressurized water system, first went critical on the 25th of February, 1962.

7
00:00:53,359 --> 00:01:04,280
By mid-summer, it was producing the 1,000 kilowatts of precise electric power needed by the three huge radars of the Sundance Air Force Station.

8
00:01:05,060 --> 00:01:10,640
These radars are under protective radomes to shield them from high mountain winds and heavy snow.

9
00:01:15,420 --> 00:01:19,859
PM1 will also supply steam to heat the entire radar installation.

10
00:01:20,859 --> 00:01:22,780
Seven million BTUs per hour.

11
00:01:23,079 --> 00:01:27,060
Heat for the operations building where the radars paint their picture of the sky.

12
00:01:27,099 --> 00:01:29,939
This picture is relayed to the air defense command.

13
00:01:32,079 --> 00:01:35,159
PM1 will heat the shops, which keep the radars working.

14
00:01:36,900 --> 00:01:41,379
As well as the station's communication equipment and other supporting facilities.

15
00:01:42,620 --> 00:01:44,780
The installation is in remote country.

16
00:01:45,840 --> 00:01:48,900
Sundance, Wyoming, the nearest settlement, is six miles away.

17
00:01:49,859 --> 00:01:52,819
At Warren Peak, neighbors are few.

18
00:01:55,799 --> 00:02:00,359
PM1 was placed here to prove that it could function in isolation,

19
00:02:00,359 --> 00:02:03,879
in a climate nearly as rigorous as that at the poles.

20
00:02:06,340 --> 00:02:12,579
At 6,000 feet above the sea, the temperature ranges from highs of 87 degrees Fahrenheit

21
00:02:12,579 --> 00:02:16,060
to lows of minus 50.

22
00:02:16,060 --> 00:02:19,520
But the radars must read the skies in any weather.

23
00:02:19,520 --> 00:02:25,340
and PM1 will furnish them power for two years from a single nuclear fuel loading.

24
00:02:25,780 --> 00:02:28,719
This reduces the need for heavy logistic support.

25
00:02:30,320 --> 00:02:36,860
Supplies reach the base by road, 93 miles overland from the railhead at Rapid City.

26
00:02:41,379 --> 00:02:45,719
The basic plant was assembled at the site from 16 packages.

27
00:02:46,460 --> 00:02:48,360
It could be relocated the same way.

28
00:02:49,520 --> 00:02:59,500
Four packages contain miscellaneous equipment, but the heart of the PM-1 is in the remaining 12 packages divided into the primary and secondary systems.

29
00:03:01,939 --> 00:03:05,200
The primary system is made up of three of these packages.

30
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:13,879
There are four tanks, reactor, steam generator, and spent fuel core tanks grouped together.

31
00:03:14,200 --> 00:03:19,000
The radioactive waste disposal tank is a part of the third package.

32
00:03:19,520 --> 00:03:21,280
It is shipped in the spent fuel tank.

33
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:25,540
The secondary system contains nine packages.

34
00:03:25,540 --> 00:03:31,620
The control room package contains the console from which the plant is run by a single controls operator.

35
00:03:32,240 --> 00:03:37,540
These controls must meet a reliability specification of 99.45%.

36
00:03:38,080 --> 00:03:41,480
Consequently, solid state components are employed.

37
00:03:42,340 --> 00:03:47,060
The turbine generator package houses the equipment that converts to electrical energy,

38
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:55,460
the heat generated by the reactor core. The generator produces 1250 kilowatts gross output.

39
00:03:55,460 --> 00:04:02,599
Equipment in the switchgear package works with the generator to refine this output and to give

40
00:04:02,599 --> 00:04:07,819
the plant one of its most striking design characteristics, the high quality of the

41
00:04:07,819 --> 00:04:10,819
electricity produced.

42
00:04:14,900 --> 00:04:19,659
This quality is governed by a voltage regulator and static exciter which can

43
00:04:19,659 --> 00:04:27,279
eliminate the need for further electrical refinement. With these units

44
00:04:27,279 --> 00:04:34,480
electrical variations are held to tight tolerances. Voltage varies less than 2%,

45
00:04:34,480 --> 00:04:45,180
percent, frequency less than two percent, harmonics less than two percent. The heat

46
00:04:45,180 --> 00:04:50,740
transfer equipment package is made of two units. One contains the evaporator

47
00:04:50,740 --> 00:04:56,379
reboiler which manufactures the low-pressure steam for space heat. The

48
00:04:56,379 --> 00:05:02,379
other unit is conventional heat exchanger equipment. Four direct air to

49
00:05:02,379 --> 00:05:07,779
steam condensers account for two packages of the system. They cool the steam from the

50
00:05:07,779 --> 00:05:15,500
turbine by drawing air over the condenser piping. No cooling liquid is involved. This

51
00:05:15,500 --> 00:05:19,659
type of condenser was selected so that the plant can operate in an area with a low water

52
00:05:19,659 --> 00:05:27,939
supply. The maintenance package holds standby generating equipment and a shop with a grinder,

53
00:05:27,939 --> 00:05:32,839
welder and lathe. Almost any general repair to the plant can be made here.

54
00:05:32,839 --> 00:05:37,439
By specification, the plant can only be shut down 21 days per year

55
00:05:37,439 --> 00:05:41,079
and of these only six are scheduled for annual plant

56
00:05:41,079 --> 00:05:45,819
shut down. The shop will help the plant to meet its shut down specification.

57
00:05:45,819 --> 00:05:52,819
A separate building holds the ninth package of the secondary system,

58
00:05:53,379 --> 00:05:57,879
the decontamination and water chemistry unit. Here too,

59
00:05:57,879 --> 00:06:04,219
Health Physics sets its line of demarcation establishing the contaminated and clean areas.

60
00:06:04,219 --> 00:06:16,480
Personnel crossing this line from the primary system are given a radiation count. We are now

61
00:06:16,480 --> 00:06:27,699
ready to look at the design of the system in some detail. 741 nuclear fuel tubes make

62
00:06:27,699 --> 00:06:34,379
up the reactor core. These tubes are grouped into seven fuel bundles, six

63
00:06:34,379 --> 00:06:40,699
peripheral and a center bundle. With the proper tools we can fuel and refuel the

64
00:06:40,699 --> 00:06:46,539
core as a whole, or if necessary we can replace individual bundles without

65
00:06:46,539 --> 00:06:55,139
removing the entire core. The core, a thermal shield and an upper skirt are

66
00:06:55,139 --> 00:06:58,139
are enclosed in a pressure vessel.

67
00:06:58,139 --> 00:07:04,639
Primary water flows into the pressure vessel, down around the core, cooling the thermal shield.

68
00:07:04,639 --> 00:07:07,740
This water then passes up through the core, absorbing

69
00:07:07,740 --> 00:07:13,079
heat, and flows out the holes of the upper skirt.

70
00:07:13,079 --> 00:07:17,759
The primary water is conveyed to the tube side of the vertical steam generator.

71
00:07:17,759 --> 00:07:21,039
It is pumped back by the primary coolant pump

72
00:07:21,040 --> 00:07:26,080
at a rate of 2,125 gallons per minute.

73
00:07:26,080 --> 00:07:30,879
Water leaves the reactor at 479 degrees Fahrenheit.

74
00:07:30,879 --> 00:07:35,220
It returns to the core at 447 degrees.

75
00:07:35,220 --> 00:07:38,259
A 32 degree rise in temperature means

76
00:07:38,259 --> 00:07:43,400
that the reactor generates nearly 35 million BTUs.

77
00:07:43,400 --> 00:07:47,140
A pressurizer maintains the system at 1,300 PSI

78
00:07:47,140 --> 00:07:49,720
to prevent boiling.

79
00:07:49,720 --> 00:07:53,500
As the primary water flows into the tube side of the steam generator,

80
00:07:53,500 --> 00:07:56,660
it gives up heat and flows out.

81
00:07:56,660 --> 00:08:00,540
Secondary feed water picks up that heat on the shell side

82
00:08:00,540 --> 00:08:05,140
and is released as dry steam.

83
00:08:05,140 --> 00:08:08,740
This steam drives a single extraction turbine generator

84
00:08:08,740 --> 00:08:12,580
and feeds the evaporator reboiler at the same time.

85
00:08:12,580 --> 00:08:17,480
Exhaust steam from the turbine flows to four air-to-steam condensers

86
00:08:17,480 --> 00:08:21,660
and is converted to water which is drained to the hot well along with the evaporator

87
00:08:21,660 --> 00:08:28,660
condensate. The remainder of the secondary loop is somewhat conventional, having the

88
00:08:29,920 --> 00:08:36,920
necessary pumps and heat exchangers to recycle feed water back to the steam generator. The

89
00:08:36,919 --> 00:08:47,639
The fuel elements are basic components of PM1. Their manufacture starts our survey of PM1

90
00:08:47,639 --> 00:08:54,899
fabrication and testing. The fuel element tubes are approximately one-half inch in outside diameter

91
00:08:54,899 --> 00:09:03,599
and 33 inches long, of which 30 inches is a fissionable U-235. We begin with the uranium

92
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:11,720
powder. Each fuel element tube contains 40 grams of enriched uranium-235. It is

93
00:09:11,720 --> 00:09:18,519
mixed with powdered stainless steel and formed into a rough cohesive sheet.

94
00:09:21,820 --> 00:09:27,220
After the sheet is centered and enclosed with stainless steel foil, this is heated

95
00:09:27,220 --> 00:09:34,980
and rolled. This is the cement meat of the fuel element. The sheet is formed into tubes

96
00:09:34,980 --> 00:09:43,639
in several steps. After its seam is closed, it is given inner and outer stainless steel

97
00:09:43,639 --> 00:09:56,600
cladding. The assembled tube is bonded and strengthened by drawing and isostatic pressure

98
00:09:56,600 --> 00:10:05,540
techniques. Tubes were assembled into the core configuration and tested in the

99
00:10:05,540 --> 00:10:09,000
company's critical facility.

100
00:10:14,860 --> 00:10:19,440
Critical tests at zero power were used to check out the nuclear efficiency of

101
00:10:19,440 --> 00:10:25,220
various core configurations and to test control characteristics. The chain

102
00:10:25,220 --> 00:10:30,920
reaction has begun a test configuration of the PM1 core achieved criticality for

103
00:10:30,920 --> 00:10:37,100
the first time on March 17, 1960. These criticality tests gave engineers the

104
00:10:37,100 --> 00:10:41,360
basis for refining their design of the core configuration and checked out the

105
00:10:41,360 --> 00:10:46,220
effectiveness of the components that control reactivity in the core. The final

106
00:10:46,220 --> 00:10:53,120
configuration contains 741 fuel elements. Its diameter just under two feet. Its

107
00:10:53,120 --> 00:10:55,399
Its active length, 30 inches.

108
00:10:55,399 --> 00:10:58,340
Its overall length, 33 inches.

109
00:10:58,340 --> 00:11:02,539
90 boron poison elements are permanently installed in the core.

110
00:11:02,539 --> 00:11:06,019
These burnable elements absorb surplus neutrons released

111
00:11:06,019 --> 00:11:08,259
by the fission process.

112
00:11:08,259 --> 00:11:12,560
They decrease the reactivity of the operating core to a controllable level.

113
00:11:17,519 --> 00:11:21,639
Y-shaped control rods start, stop, and control

114
00:11:21,639 --> 00:11:29,019
rate of reactivity. The Y rods contain europium oxide stabilized with titanium

115
00:11:29,019 --> 00:11:34,720
oxide and mixed with stainless steel powder to form a cermet. There are six of

116
00:11:34,720 --> 00:11:42,639
these rods in the core. When all of the six rods are fully inserted, the reactor

117
00:11:42,639 --> 00:11:48,659
is subcritical. Fission cannot take place. As a safety margin, the core is

118
00:11:48,659 --> 00:11:52,860
is subcritical with only five rods fully inserted,

119
00:11:52,860 --> 00:11:57,899
or even with four rods inserted, and two in the operating position.

120
00:11:57,899 --> 00:12:05,120
When all six are withdrawn, a point is reached at which the reaction is slightly supercritical.

121
00:12:05,120 --> 00:12:11,939
Then the rods are repositioned at the critical point to hold the level of reaction constant.

122
00:12:11,939 --> 00:12:22,500
When the rods are reinserted fully, reactor becomes subcritical, shutting it down. The rod movement is controlled by

123
00:12:22,500 --> 00:12:30,579
magnetic jacks. When coils in these jacks are energized they hold or move the rods.

124
00:12:30,579 --> 00:12:36,779
When energized sequentially they move the rods by increments. Gravity and

125
00:12:36,779 --> 00:12:42,600
springs in the top of the rod housing will drop the rods if the current is cut.

126
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:49,860
Loss of current scrams the reactor, a failsafe feature. Moreover, these jacks

127
00:12:49,860 --> 00:12:54,820
require only static seals, mainly on the pressure vessel head. No part moves

128
00:12:54,820 --> 00:13:01,899
against the seal, so the likelihood of leakage is minimized. As we have seen,

129
00:13:01,899 --> 00:13:07,160
pressurized water in the core acts as a moderator of neutrons for the fission

130
00:13:07,159 --> 00:13:15,159
process. The same water transfers the heat generated in the reactor to the

131
00:13:15,159 --> 00:13:21,079
steam generator. With this quarter scale flow test engineers studied the patterns

132
00:13:21,079 --> 00:13:29,419
of water moving through the reactor. PM1 packages have been designed so that all

133
00:13:29,419 --> 00:13:34,639
welding is done at the factory. Field welding is eliminated because flanged

134
00:13:34,639 --> 00:13:41,699
fittings will be used for connections to be made at the site. PM1 was completely

135
00:13:41,699 --> 00:13:46,740
packaged at the contractor's plant. The packages were interconnected and tested

136
00:13:46,740 --> 00:13:53,600
before shipment. All 16 packages of the PM1 system are built to withstand the

137
00:13:53,600 --> 00:14:01,759
stress of airlift. The package dimensions are eight feet eight inches by eight

138
00:14:01,759 --> 00:14:07,360
feet 8 inches by 30 feet long. The maximum weight of the packages has been

139
00:14:07,360 --> 00:14:12,740
set at 30,000 pounds. Set on the basis of the permissible load that can be carried

140
00:14:12,740 --> 00:14:20,980
on a C-130 aircraft on a thousand mile mission. Air transportability of the

141
00:14:20,980 --> 00:14:26,080
system was flight tested during the spring of 1960. This airlift was a high

142
00:14:26,080 --> 00:14:31,519
point of the Air Force participation in the PM1 project. The Air Force also

143
00:14:31,519 --> 00:14:36,019
contributed project officers to the program and tested the system condensers

144
00:14:36,019 --> 00:14:45,279
in the environmental hangars at Eglin Air Force Base. Beginning May 29th 1961,

145
00:14:45,279 --> 00:14:50,980
C-130 aircraft flew PM-1 packages to Ellsworth Air Force Base, South Dakota

146
00:14:50,980 --> 00:14:55,759
for the overland trip to Warren Peak.

147
00:15:01,519 --> 00:15:20,279
The PM-1 was reassembled at the site on previously prepared foundations.

148
00:15:20,279 --> 00:15:24,939
The four tanks of the primary system were erected on foundations 30 feet below floor

149
00:15:24,939 --> 00:15:27,139
level.

150
00:15:27,139 --> 00:15:32,740
fill of crushed rock is packed around the tanks as a shield to reduce radiation to a safe level.

151
00:15:45,899 --> 00:15:52,299
Once package interconnections were complete and the core had been installed, pre-startup

152
00:15:52,300 --> 00:15:56,620
checkout and testing was accomplished. Sub systems were aligned in preparation

153
00:15:56,620 --> 00:16:04,620
for PM1 to take over its role as power plant for the site. The auxiliary systems

154
00:16:04,620 --> 00:16:10,840
have been started and we're ready to go critical. The rods are withdrawn in

155
00:16:10,840 --> 00:16:17,480
pre-calculated amounts and we watch for the start of a chain reaction. The

156
00:16:17,480 --> 00:16:21,820
reactor period is oscillating from positive to negative each time the rods

157
00:16:21,820 --> 00:16:32,800
rods are withdrawn. Now it remains slightly positive. We are critical. We adjust the control

158
00:16:32,800 --> 00:16:38,980
rods to establish the proper heating rate. The coolant water is continuously sampled

159
00:16:38,980 --> 00:16:45,980
so that its chemical balance can be corrected. We are up to operating pressure and temperature,

160
00:16:45,980 --> 00:16:57,820
to generate steam. Steam to the turbine. We have the turbine up to speed.

161
00:17:00,759 --> 00:17:07,240
Now apply field voltage to the generator and adjust it. Power on the tie line.

162
00:17:07,240 --> 00:17:15,299
PM1 is in operation. Two men can operate this plant. One man monitors the

163
00:17:15,299 --> 00:17:22,220
plant's operation at the console and the other continually inspects the working

164
00:17:22,220 --> 00:17:28,519
parts. The entire PM-1 crew has been trained for every conceivable situation

165
00:17:28,519 --> 00:17:35,180
arising in normal operation, in emergencies, or in maintenance. PM-1 is a

166
00:17:35,180 --> 00:17:40,440
safe system. Safety is built into the fundamentals of the design. PM-1 is a

167
00:17:40,440 --> 00:17:45,079
pressurized water system. If the water moderator in the reactor is overheated,

168
00:17:45,079 --> 00:17:50,460
it must expand and when its density decreases it loses its ability to

169
00:17:50,460 --> 00:17:59,679
support the chain reaction. The reactor will shut down.

170
00:17:59,679 --> 00:18:04,960
The reactors controls are fail-safe. If current is lost the rods will scram the

171
00:18:04,960 --> 00:18:12,019
reactor. The instrumentation continuously monitors 68 points in the system.

172
00:18:12,019 --> 00:18:15,019
temperatures, pressures, and radiation.

173
00:18:18,019 --> 00:18:23,019
Solid state components ensure a high order of reliability in this instrumentation.

174
00:18:23,019 --> 00:18:27,019
The reactor safety system, which can warn the operator of potential trouble,

175
00:18:27,019 --> 00:18:30,019
also incorporates the SCRAM logic circuit.

176
00:18:30,019 --> 00:18:36,019
This is a self-monitoring device that watches for 13 specific combinations of conditions.

177
00:18:37,019 --> 00:18:40,019
Its function is instantaneous action.

178
00:18:40,019 --> 00:18:46,559
For example, in five sets of conditions it may lock the rods so that they cannot be withdrawn further.

179
00:18:47,079 --> 00:18:52,879
Or if the reactor exceeds 125% power, the circuit will scram the reactor.

180
00:18:55,779 --> 00:19:02,500
The crew has been thoroughly drilled in safety until emergency procedures and corrective action are automatic.

181
00:19:02,500 --> 00:19:12,940
A single PM-1 core will furnish full power to the radar site for two years. During this time,

182
00:19:12,940 --> 00:19:20,019
the Air Force, the Atomic Energy Commission, and Martin will scrutinize PM-1 operation. We

183
00:19:20,019 --> 00:19:26,319
will discover ways to extend the power range to increase the usefulness of such plants. Meanwhile,

184
00:19:26,319 --> 00:19:33,319
the first of a series of closely related systems, PM-3A, is being tested in the Antarctic.

185
00:19:35,240 --> 00:19:40,740
Compact and self-sufficient portable plants installed in remote regions difficult to supply

186
00:19:40,740 --> 00:19:47,119
are pioneers. PM-1 and its small crew is proving the safety and practicality of the medium

187
00:19:47,119 --> 00:19:54,119
range reactor power plant. PM-1 opens the frontier for many new applications of nuclear

188
00:19:54,120 --> 00:19:58,120
electric power, both military and civilian.
